# Game_SimonRuns — Simon Runs Competition (ID 6)
# Files: src/coordinator/Game_SimonRuns.h, Game_SimonRuns.cpp
# HTML: data/game_simonruns_setup.html, game_simonruns_names.html, game_simonruns_run.html

## GAMEPLAY
Competitive Simon Says with racing/timing. 1-3 groups compete in parallel.
Optional central display puck shared across groups. Time accumulates across levels.
Error locks group until replay.

## CONFIG
- numGroups (1-3), centralDisplay, targetLength (default 10)
- colorBlind, soundOn

## STATES per group
SIMRUN_SETUP → SIMRUN_PREPARE (3s countdown) → SIMRUN_SHOW → SIMRUN_INPUT → SIMRUN_WAITING → loop
Terminal: SIMRUN_FINISHED (rainbow) or SIMRUN_DISQUALIFIED

## KEY MECHANICS
- SHOW: display puck shows sequence (800ms on, 300ms off per color)
- INPUT: correct → advance, complete → accumulate time, level up
- Wrong input: lock group (inputLocked), red fail, 3x beeps
- Locked: press display puck to replay sequence
- Central display: shared puck coordinates multi-group play
- accumulatedTime: total time across all levels (not reset per level)
- 8 normal colors + 8 colorblind colors

## COMMANDS
setup, cfg_groups, cfg_len, cfg_central, cfg_blind, cfg_sound, preview,
start_all, start_X, stop_all, exit, disq_X

## STATUS JSON
{groups: [{id, state, locked, lvl, target, time (accumulated), prog, seq: ["#RRGGBB",...]}]}
